This repository contains no OM Digital Solutions / Olympus firmware. The patcher (patch.py) works on the official
firmware file that each user downloads themselves; releases/*/patch.json hold only the bytes this project writes
(its own code, hooks, and the picture-mode tables rearranged to list the profiles).

Based on:
- Caduceus (cakelesscoder/caduceus-ep7, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 cakelesscoder), firmware patches for the Olympus
  PEN E-P7: the idea of looks loaded from a card file, the heap state block armed at the first half-press, the
  official-firmware download request in patch.py, and the update container format as its decoder states it.
- Caduceus for OM-3 (androidfanman/caduceus-om3, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 androidfanman): the LOOKS record layout
  that the OM5F file reuses, the film looks in looklab/films.json (adapted: see that file's note), the preview
  numbers in LookLab (fitted to the OM-3 by that project), and the layout of this project's site and guides.
- The OM-5 Mark II colour-profile, Hue / Lightness, white balance, Monochrome Profile and Live ND work written for
  xulfr/oly_fw_analysis (a fork of fishcu/oly_fw_analysis) by xulfr; fishcu's PEN-F research showed the way.
  No file of fishcu's is included here.

Sample photos in looklab/samples are public domain (CC0 1.0); see looklab/samples/CREDITS.md.

Developer tools in tools/dev drive OM-Emu (github.com/flatpanda/om-emu; the E148 work is in xulfr/om-emu), which is
not included and keeps its own licence. The camera screens on the site are pictures drawn by OM-Emu running this
project's firmware; the menu design is OM Digital Solutions'.

